{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1020"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge technology/computing","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/technology__computing.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",552],["+","On 28 April 2009 Kickstarter, founded by Perry Chen, Yancey Strickler and Charles Adler, opened in New York as an internet community for funding creative projects: backers pledge money to films, games or gadgets and receive rewards if the goal is reached. In 2011 the Chinese internet company Tencent released WeChat (Weixin), a messaging app that grew into China's largest social networking platform, combining chat, a social feed and payments, and passed a billion monthly users in 2018. "],["=",216],["+","Kickstarter | 28 April 2009 | Perry Chen, Yancey Strickler, Charles Adler |\n| "],["=",21],["+","\n| WeChat | 2011 | Tencent |"],["=",120]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",514],["+","Am 28. April 2009 ging in New York Kickstarter an den Start, gegründet von Perry Chen, Yancey Strickler und Charles Adler: eine Internet-Community zur Finanzierung kreativer Projekte, bei der Unterstützer Filmen, Spielen oder technischen Geräten Geld zusagen und Gegenleistungen erhalten, wenn das Ziel erreicht wird. 2011 veröffentlichte der chinesische Internetkonzern Tencent WeChat (Weixin), eine Messenger-App, die zu Chinas größter Social-Networking-Plattform heranwuchs, Chat, sozialen Feed und Bezahlen vereint und 2018 die Marke von einer Milliarde monatlichen Nutzern überschritt. "],["=",212],["+","Kickstarter | 28. April 2009 | Perry Chen, Yancey Strickler, Charles Adler |\n| "],["=",21],["+","\n| WeChat | 2011 | Tencent |"],["=",110]]}]},
